"test":{"name":"attrition-rule-supply-chain-line","kind":"rules","opponent":"Human","rounds":"4","check":"attritionSupplyChainLine","question":"Supply through a chain of two supply units (the HQ feeds A, A feeds B, B feeds a grunt): both are linked, and the line drawn from the grunt runs through B, then A, to the HQ, each once (it used to turn back from A to B: two hubs drawn feeding each other). Two supply units next to each other far from any supply are not linked, supply nothing (not even each other), and have no line. And for every placement of two supply units near the HQ, and every one-tile move of one of them previewed, the line from each linked one ends at the HQ, passing each once.","rules":"attrition"},
